/*
 * FORM WORKFLOW - "Only One Settings Record - Settings"
 *
 *   Form         : Settings
 *   Record event : on add          <-- NOT "on add or edit". See the warning below.
 *   Trigger      : on validate     (runs BEFORE the record is inserted)
 *
 * WHY THIS EXISTS
 *   Settings is a singleton. Two things break the moment a second row exists:
 *     1. Six DAILY scheduled workflows are anchored on this form
 *        (type = schedule, form = Settings, start = Next_Workflow_Run).
 *        Creator fires a form-anchored schedule once PER RECORD, so a second
 *        row runs every one of them twice a day - duplicate lot status writes,
 *        duplicate forecast recalcs, duplicate approval emails:
 *              Test Add Hours
 *              Set Close Date - Lots
 *              Update Sold/Contracted - Forecast Year
 *              Update Actual Lots - Forecast
 *              Check for Stuck Budget Approvals
 *              Update Budgets w/ Projects Info - Budget
 *     2. The expression Settings[ID != 0] appears 24 times across the app and is
 *        consumed as a SINGLE record (e.g. sendApprovalReminders.dg line 15:
 *        settingsRec = Settings[ID != 0]; then settingsRec.Approval_Reminder_Interval_Days).
 *        With two rows that read becomes ambiguous and silently picks one.
 *
 * !! DO NOT SET THE RECORD EVENT TO "on add or edit" !!
 *   On an edit the record already exists, so Settings[ID != 0].count() returns 1,
 *   the guard would cancel every single Settings save, and the form would be
 *   permanently unusable. 25 of the 31 on-validate workflows in this app use
 *   "on add or edit" - do not copy one of those by reflex. Copy
 *   "Field Validations - Mass Create Forecasts", which is "on add".
 *
 * The input.ID branch below is belt-and-braces: if a future maintainer does flip
 * the trigger to "on add or edit", the guard excludes the record being saved
 * instead of bricking the form. On an add, input.ID is null and this degrades to
 * the plain count.
 */
existingCount = Settings[ID != 0].count();
if(input.ID != null)
{
	existingCount = Settings[ID != input.ID].count();
}
if(existingCount > 0)
{
	alert "Only one Settings record is allowed. A Settings record already exists - open Settings from the menu and edit that record instead of adding a new one.";
	cancel submit;
}
